  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies two gate-based quantum machine learning applications in finance: quantum DPP sampling for churn prediction on IBM Guadalupe (16 qubits) and quantum orthogonal/compound neural-network inference for SME credit risk on IBM Hanoi (8 qubits). The reported quantitative results are 77.5% precision for DPP-RF versus 71.6% for the Random Forest baseline, 62.77% vs 61.42% withdrawals captured, and credit-risk Gini scores of 54.29% (OrthoResNN), 53.95% (ExpResNN), with hardware inference dropping to 50.19% and 40.20% respectively before mitigation improved OrthoResNN to 53.68%.",
